Mutant: a start that removes a last segment without an indexed transaction cuts or creates a segment before the removal is synced. Must fail: the start syncs the directory after it removes a torn last segment, before it cuts the segment before it; a last segment without an index file is removed, the directory synced, and the segment created again from its header; a first segment with a torn header is removed, the directory synced, and the spool starts again.
Apply from the repository root with git apply, and never commit it applied.

--- a/src/bin/pgcopydb/ld_spool.c
+++ b/src/bin/pgcopydb/ld_spool.c
@@ -2304,8 +2304,7 @@
 
 	/* the index file first, as cleanup does, and on disk before create, which uses O_EXCL */
 	if (start->removed &&
-		(!unlink_file(start->last.index) || !unlink_file(start->last.segment.filename) ||
-		 !spool_sync_directory(dirname)))
+		(!unlink_file(start->last.index) || !unlink_file(start->last.segment.filename)))
 	{
 		return false;
 	}
